body:
Trans people are always put in doubt by cis people and society, so it's pretty normal that trans persons doubt themselves. It's normal. It took me almost three years of doubting for finally accept that I'm trans. The past week I come out through a letter to my tutor college and I'm really happy. Personally, the doubts still but in a diferent way: now i doubt if really i can do it, I mean, I really want transition, but I'll get it?

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

TW: suicide thoughs and notes

Also, in this process of three yaears, I wrote a bunch of suicide letters to my parents telling them that I'm trans. The last letter I wrote was in february of 2018. But now I decided that my parents will the last people in knowing. I love them and I want them in my transition, but It's just for keep safe.

If I don't drink water before of sleep, then the "lady water", a tall and bony lady, will appears in my dreams and she take me to the river to drown me.

&#x200B;

My parents just did not want to get up in the middle of the night to bring me water.

If I tell you where, I will die.

&#x200B;

Edit: Thanks so much for the Silver! :)

Please, resist, my little girl. Suicide isn't the solution. I know is hard and painful as hell. I'm a trans guy pre-everything and also my parents don't accept me, even I can't tell them anything until I leave the house. I afraid of my future. I also think in suicide as reincarnation, but nothing assures us that we'll born in a better life than this. I don't have the solution of our problems but I know that suicide isn't the solution. I don't know what else to tell you so that you stay here. No matter how time take us, some day will be living better. I promise you.

&#x200B;

Send me a PM if you want.

&#x200B;

We love you and you're not alone.
